                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2f5e24bc-205e-37f4-baaf-315bec63f4ec",
                        "entry_id": "3163d05b-fc1a-3344-8c95-5cfb2f4f7f6c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A parish constable, a uniformed minor (lay) official, who ushers and keeps order."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d6116b33-7e3c-4f31-891b-c37f948ea2f9",
                                "sense_id": "2f5e24bc-205e-37f4-baaf-315bec63f4ec",
                                "text": "Twas on a holy Thursday, their innocent faces clean,\nThe children walking two and two in red and blue and green:\nGrey-headed beadles walked before, with wands as white as snow,\nTill into the high dome of Paul's they like Thames waters flow."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "63182af7-6968-4bcc-84c3-9fbc2bbf9ff1",
                                "sense_id": "2f5e24bc-205e-37f4-baaf-315bec63f4ec",
                                "text": "The beadle […] generally understood in the neighbourhood to be a ridiculous institution […] The policeman considers him an imbecile civilian, a remnant of the barbarous watchmen times, but gives him admission as something that must be borne with until government shall abolish him."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ad605b91-8400-443d-aaaa-a6281efbc552",
                                "sense_id": "2f5e24bc-205e-37f4-baaf-315bec63f4ec",
                                "text": "Yes, yes, begad—of course you go out with him—it’s like the country, you know; everybody goes out with everybody in the Gardens, and there are beadles, you know, and that sort of thing—everybody walks in the Temple Gardens."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8241a12d-e56e-49d1-bfab-b57f13c78af4",
                                "sense_id": "2f5e24bc-205e-37f4-baaf-315bec63f4ec",
                                "text": "His face expressed horror and indignation. Instinct rather than reason came to my help; he was a Beadle; I was a woman."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "21fc2b59-ad45-362d-abca-239cb2053401",
                        "entry_id": "3163d05b-fc1a-3344-8c95-5cfb2f4f7f6c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An attendant to the minister."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Scotland"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
